  "result": "The absence feature is in place across the schema, migration, repository, service, assignment, overdue, mention, and removal paths. Typecheck, lint, and the full suite pass (74 files, 649 tests).\n\nChoices I made that you may want to redirect:\n- The end-after-start rule is a `.refine` on `setAbsenceSchema`. The object shape is unchanged, so client forms reject a bad range too. The service also checks it, and throws a plain `Error`, which `toAppError` maps to `internal_error`.\n- Overdue alerts resolve the delegate at the sweep's `occurredAt`. The sweep itself is untouched.\n- The mention rule is one hop, with dedupe and author exclusion handled by the existing `notify`.\n- No server actions or UI were added, since the spec only lists service exports.\n- The new cases are in `tests/services/member-absence.test.ts`, plus schema cases in `tests/schemas/member.schema.test.ts`.",
